# 1. IT Service Management (ITSM)

## What is ITSM?

IT Service Management (ITSM) is an approach used to deliver, manage, support, and improve IT services to meet business and user needs.

Examples of IT services include:

- Email and Microsoft 365
- Company laptops and desktops
- Network and Wi-Fi connectivity
- Shared folders and file access
- Business applications
- User account management

## Why Do Organizations Use ITSM?

- Improve IT service quality.
- Track incidents and service requests.
- Assign responsibilities to support teams.
- Prioritize issues based on business impact.
- Monitor service targets.
- Maintain documentation and accountability.
- Identify recurring issues and opportunities for improvement.

## Common ITSM Tools

Examples include ServiceNow, Jira Service Management, and Freshservice.

These platforms help support teams record, assign, track, and manage tickets.

